#!/usr/bin/python3
#
# pitcrew-gui — a desktop front-end for pitcrew, in the shape of GNOME System
# Monitor: a component list and a Resources view of live CPU/RAM graphs.
#
# It owns NO measurement logic. Everything on screen comes from
# `pitcrew json --watch`, which is the same snapshot the terminal dashboard
# draws — so the two can never disagree, and a fix in lib/03a-snapshot.sh lands
# in both. The GUI is a renderer and a set of buttons, nothing more.
#
# The interpreter is pinned to /usr/bin/python3 rather than `env python3` on
# purpose: a Homebrew or pyenv python earlier on $PATH has no `gi`, and the
# failure (ModuleNotFoundError at launch, from the app grid, with no terminal
# attached) is invisible. The system python is the one with the GTK bindings.
"""GTK4/libadwaita front-end over `pitcrew json --watch`."""

